  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Using Drones and Early Warning Systems for Pre- and Post-Floods Disast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gambia is located within the drainage basin of the Gambia River and is susceptible to hazards such as riverine flooding, flash floods, and other challenges. Floods affect the livelihoods of more than 70% of the population in the country. The standard response is a post-catastrophe crisis management because of inadequate forecasting and alert capabilities. We propose with the Gambian Government to deploy drones and improved early warning systems to reduce the impact of flood disaster in the Gambia. Drones will help in long-term climate risk assessments, mapping of safe and unsafe sites, and evacuation routes. The alert systems would contribute to the enhancement of flood risk management.</narrative>
  </description>
